mount: make "mount -a" and fstab remounts work the way OpenRC uses them.

- -O: OpenRC's localmount runs "mount -a -t noproc,<netfs> -O no_netdev".
  toybox treated -O as "the entry must carry this literal option", so no
  fstab entry ever matched, mount -a mounted nothing and exited 0, and
  /boot, /tmp and tracefs were never mounted.  Use util-linux semantics:
  "noOPT" means OPT is absent, "+OPT" is literal, anything else present.
- -a skips entries that are already mounted by comparing device numbers
  as well as names, and always treats "/" as mounted: /proc/mounts calls
  a kernel-mounted root "/dev/root", so the root entry was mounted again.
- -o remount DEV DIR (OpenRC's "fstabinfo --remount") matches the
  mountpoint instead of DEV against /proc/mounts' "/dev/root", so fstab
  root options (noatime, errors=remount-ro) are applied.  The last of
  noatime/relatime wins, since remount starts from /proc/mounts' options.
- remount walks /proc/mounts as both lists; CONFIG_TOYBOX_FREE freed it
  twice and crashed silently.
- Resolve LABEL= as well as UUID= (with toybox's own blkid: reforger's
  blkid on $PATH has no -U/-L), and PARTUUID=/PARTLABEL=.  There is no
  udev, so PARTUUID= reads the MBR disk signature or the GPT partition
  GUID of the parent disk found via /sys/class/block.
- "noauto" was never recognized (comma_scan() reads it as no+"auto"), and
  fstab-only options (noauto, nofail, _netdev, users, x-*, comment=) went
  to the kernel, which rejects them with EINVAL.
- -t "noproc,nfs,...": later list items compared only len-2 characters,
  so "nfs" excluded every type starting with "n" (ntfs, ntfs3, nilfs2).
- A swap entry was swapon'ed and then also handed to mount(2); stop there.

